# Separate problems, separate tickets

The incident page describes one cause, but the desk's classification distinguishes a shared parser problem from a conflicting booking form hint. Group by cause and tenant context, rather than subject alone. Check the evidence before treating the classification as a confirmed diagnosis.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Parser

Engineering reports this fixed on 5 October: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

The shared parser reads dates month-first for day-first tenants. Confirm the entered date, tenant locale, and resulting booking before filing a report here.

## Booking-v3 hint

Engineering marked this won’t fix on 5 October because the booking-v3 form was retired.

For day-first tenants, booking-v3 presents a month-first hint while the form reads the date using the tenant's locale. The hint and parser should agree with that locale.

## One-day moves

The table notes reports read as a one-day move but filed by tenant under the parser. A one-day shift does not establish a month/day swap; retain these reports in the current classification and investigate the original date, time, time zone, and calendar display before assigning a separate cause.

## Queue and triage

The desk's export is a snapshot. Received and merged dates differ; check both when assessing the queue. Subject matches alone can merge distinct causes and split matching ones.

